<Layout title="Editorial Policy" description="How Trade90 sources official policy decisions, explains calculations and corrects data." canonical="/editorial-policy/">
<main class="wrap"><article class="article"><header class="page-intro"><span class="eyebrow">Sources and corrections</span><h1>Editorial Policy</h1><p>Trade90 aims to make public rate information understandable while clearly distinguishing observed data from expectations and interpretation.</p></header>
<h2>Official source first</h2><p>Published central-bank policy rates are documented with a benchmark definition, decision date, effective date and a link to a source publication. We preserve original dates rather than presenting old observations as current market events.</p>
<h2>Calculations</h2><p>Rate gaps are calculated deterministically and tested for all 28 combinations. Read the <a href="/methodology/">methodology</a> for the signed spread formula, ranking method and differing national benchmark conventions.</p>
<h2>Forward estimates</h2><p>Expected rate gaps must originate from verifiable, appropriately licensed, timestamped market inputs. Central-bank remarks, AI-generated interpretations and opinions are not substitutes for genuine implied forward pricing.</p>
<h2>Changes and causality</h2><p>We separate actual policy-rate decisions from market repricing of expectations. We do not assert a financial price reaction was caused by one economic release unless the evidence supports that explanation.</p>
<h2>Data cadence and licenses</h2><p>Official benchmark snapshots, central-bank calendars and publications currently use dated curation, not automatic live refresh. We do not call unlicensed third-party quotes a live feed. See our <a href="/data-policy/">public data sources, update practices and license safeguards</a>.</p><h2>Corrections</h2><p>To report a source, date or calculation error, email <a href="mailto:admin@tradeninety.com">admin@tradeninety.com</a> with the page, affected figure and authoritative reference.</p></article></main>
</Layout>
